WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.240
Let's explore the system level settings

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:08.080
in HAXcms. So from our site dashboard,

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:10.240
if we click on our little user profile

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.320
icon, we can see that we could toggle

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.480
dark mode, sound effects, but let's go

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.400
to settings.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.840
From settings, we can view skeletons,

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:23.600
themes, media, third party integrations,

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.480
and down the road, blocks, global CSS

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.199
and JavaScript, and a style guide. But

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:32.000
to start, let's review status. Status is

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.520
going to tell us the latest version that

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.600
we're on

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.000
versus what exists in the world as the

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.559
highest new version, what our server is

00:00:40.559 --> 00:00:42.960
running, and we'll also indicate if

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.200
there's any misconfigurations on the

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:49.520
file system that are needed.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.800
Under skeletons, we can limit which

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.320
skeletons

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.360
or site creation tools exist. So if I

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.920
check these ones on and save,

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.720
we'll have more templates available. So

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:07.600
the templating tool in HAXcms is our

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.680
skeletons. If we want to take a site,

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.760
download it, and turn it into a skeleton

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.920
that other users can select or that we

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.920
can select in the future, then that's

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:21.040
where we would perform this action.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.799
There's themes where we can do similar

00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:25.680
where we can disable certain themes.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:27.360
media where we can set some media

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:30.000
policies associated with image size,

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.439
image quality, acceptable formats and

00:01:33.439 --> 00:01:35.280
thirdparty integrations which is still

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.840
being built out for AI, YouTube and the

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:39.840
future.
